(4099458, 581928, 6172, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the win!  I had to laugh at your technique (30 sec., no tripod).  Just goes to show how you can make great images with less equipment.</td>', 'Congrats on the win!  I had to laugh at your technique (30 sec., no tripod).  Just goes to show how you can make great images with less equipment.', '2007-09-18 18:10:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4107113, 580434, 78132, '<td valign="top">So very beautiful...a dreamland!</td>', 'So very beautiful...a dreamland!', '2007-09-21 14:16:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(4109617, 581802, 83484, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  For those that didn''t see the power, sorry, will try better next time.  Might be a bit advanced, but this particular radar has a transmitter with a maximum output of approximately 750 kW, or approximately 700 average countertop microwaves operating at full power at the same time.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  For those that didn''t see the power, sorry, will try better next time.  Might be a bit advanced, but this particular radar has a transmitter with a maximum output of approximately 750 kW, or approximately 700 average countertop microwaves operating at full power at the same time.', '2007-09-22 23:44:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4112064, 580661, 3724, '<td valign="top">looming skeletal spiral - most interesting architecture &amp; excellent off center pov.</td>', 'looming skeletal spiral - most interesting architecture & excellent off center pov.', '2007-09-24 09:30:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4168854, 580683, 57421, '<td valign="top">what are the odds? it was close. Had you submitted the 5108 one, you cou have a ruined it all with a blue ;)<br/> <br/>great photo, congrats on the ribbon.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-10-15 10:14:23.</i></td>', 'what are the odds? it was close. Had you submitted the 5108 one, you cou have a ruined it all with a blue ;) great photo, congrats on the ribbon.', '2007-10-15 11:13:46.000000', '2007-10-15 11:14:23.000000', 0),
(4169639, 581636, 30982, '<td valign="top">Good action, good editing.  To have a great action shot, one needs to have something in sharp focus for most viewers.  For composition, it''s a bit cramped on the left side, and for DPC viewers, there''s the clutter factor with the cars and such in the background.  No way to get rid of those things other than by trying to find an angle that doesn''t include them (which in situations like this is vitually impossible unless you can get high and shoot down.)  Not sure what you mean by shadows/highlights pushed it to the limit - looks pretty balanced to me.  You have a good grasp of basic editing techniques - not sure how much help I can be in that respect!</td>', 'Good action, good editing.  To have a great action shot, one needs to have something in sharp focus for most viewers.  For composition, it''s a bit cramped on the left side, and for DPC viewers, there''s the clutter factor with the cars and such in the background.  No way to get rid of those things other than by trying to find an angle that doesn''t include them (which in situations like this is vitually impossible unless you can get high and shoot down.)  Not sure what you mean by shadows/highlights pushed it to the limit - looks pretty balanced to me.  You have a good grasp of basic editing techniques - not sure how much help I can be in that respect!', '2007-10-15 16:46:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4177475, 582433, 48560, '<td valign="top">your prediction is way off - now go into your room and reflect why you cant create a 5.7 submission properly! hehe...</td>', 'your prediction is way off - now go into your room and reflect why you cant create a 5.7 submission properly! hehe...', '2007-10-18 03:07:02.000000', NULL, 0),
